---
title: Matcha Cheesecake
servings: 8
image: https://recipeflame.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/12/Matcha-Green-Tea-Cheesecake.webp
---

== Crust ==

Preheat oven to 350°F.

Using a #food processor{}, blend @graham crackers{1.75%packages} into a powder.

Mix the graham crackers with @butter{1%stick}(unsalted, melted), @sugar{3%tbsp}, and @matcha{}(to taste) with a spatula.

Place a #10" glass pie pan{} on a baking sheet.

Press the crust mixture into the pie pan to form the shape of a crust.

Bake for ~{5%minutes} at 350°F, then set aside to cool.

== Filling ==

Set the oven temperature to 325°F. You may want to let the oven cool for a bit first to ensure the proper temperature.

Using a #stand mixer{}, gently beat @cream cheese{3%8oz packages}(softened) until smooth.

Add @sugar{1%cup} and continue to beat until well combined.

Add in @eggs{3}, one at a time, until a creamy batter forms.

Mix in @sour cream{1%cup}(an 8oz container), @all-purpose flour{2%tbsp}, @matcha{5%tsp}(I have a sweet and bitter matcha, I like to do 1 tsp bitter, 4 tsp sweet), and @vanilla extract{1%tsp} until batter is smooth.

Pour the batter over the crust, spreading gently and evenly, ensuring there are no air pockets or bubbles.

Bake at 325°F for ~{50-60%minutes}. 

> The edges should mostly be set, but the cheesecake should still jiggle, especially in the middle.

Allow the cheesecake to set in the oven with the door slightly ajar for around ~{60%minutes}.

Refrigerate for at least 4 hours, but ideally overnight.

Top with @?matcha{1%tsp} before serving.

> I -wanted- to follow this recipe, but it requires a springform pan, water bath, etc. and thus is more complicated: https://www.reddit.com/r/food/comments/9jj8qp/homemade_matcha_cheesecake/?rdt=49801 . Instead, I settled on merging our normal cheesecake recipes with this one: https://senbirdtea.com/blogs/recipes/a-matcha-green-tea-cheesecake-recipe-worth-celebrating